><non-patent-citations><nplcit status="new"><text>See also references of EP     1186651A1</text><sources><source name="SEA" created-by-npl="N"/></sources></nplcit></non-patent-citations></citations></technical-data><parties><applicants><applicant status="new" format="epo"><addressbook><name>KAO CORP</name><address><country>JP</country></address></addressbook></applicant><applicant status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>KAO CORPORATION</name></addressbook></applicant></applicants><inventors><inventor status="new" format="epo"><addressbook><name>NITTA HIDEICHI</name></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="epo"><addressbook><name>SAIJO HIROYUKI</name></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="epo"><addressbook><name>TAKAYA HITOSHI</name></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="epo"><addressbook><name>YAMAGUCHI SHU</name></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="epo"><addressbook><name>YAMASHITA HIROYUKI</name></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>NITTA, HIDEICHI</name></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>SAIJO, HIROYUKI</name></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>TAKAYA, HITOSHI</name></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>YAMAGUCHI, SHU</name></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>YAMASHITA, HIROYUKI</name></addressbook></inventor></inventors></parties></bibliographic-data><abstract load-source="docdb" source="national office" status="new" lang="EN"><p>A particulate detergent which comprises 5 to 50 wt.% phosphate builder, 5 to 40 wt.% anionic surfactant, and 1 to 30 wt.% nonionic surfactant and has an average particle diameter of 150 to 500  mu , a bulk density of 500 g/L or higher, and a flow time of 10 seconds or shorter, wherein the particulate detergent comprises detergent particles each capable of releasing, from inner parts thereof, bubbles having a diameter of at least one-tenth the particle diameter during dissolution in water and has a solubility as calculated with equation (1) of 90% or higher. Since the particulate detergent has enhanced solubility and flowability, it can have improved suitability for laundering by hand. Equation (1) Solubility (%) = [1-(T/S)]x100 S: Amount of added particles for detergent addition (g) T: Dry amount of residue on sieve after stirring (g).</p></abstract><abstract load-source="docdb" source="national office" status="new" lang="FR"><p>L'invention porte sur un détergent particulaire comportant de 5 à 50 % en poids de phosphate, de 5 à 40 % en poids d'un tensio-actif anionique, de 1 à 30 % en poids de tensio-actif non anionique, et dont le diamètre moyen des particules est compris entre 150 et 500  mu m, le poids volumique, de 500g/l ou plus, et le temps d'écoulement, de 10 s ou moins. Les particules du détergent peuvent dégager de leurs parties internes lors de leur dissolution dans l'eau des bulles d'un diamètre au moins égal à un dixième de leur diamètre, et leur solubilité, calculée selon l'équation (1), est de 90 % ou plus. Les qualités renforcées de solubilité et de flottabilité dudit détergent en améliorent l'aptitude au lavage à la main. L'équation (1) a la forme suivante: solubilité (%) = [1-(T/S)] x 100, S étant la quantité de particules ajoutées par adjonction de détergent (g), et T, la quantité de résidus restant sur le tamis après brassage (g).</p></abstract><copyright>User acknowledges that the Information Retrieval Facility (IRF) and its third party providers retain all right, title and interest in and to this xml under applicable copyright laws. User acquires no ownership rights to this xml including but not limited to its format. User hereby accepts the terms and conditions of the Licence Agreement set forth at http://www.ir-facility.org/legal/marec/d